# CURSOR RULE: Media SDK Headless UI Layer (@media-sdk/ui-react)

## ARCHITECTURAL PURPOSE
`@media-sdk/ui-react` is a **STRICTLY HEADLESS** UI library using the **Prop-Getters Pattern** (similar to Downshift or React Table). It contains ZERO CSS, ZERO Tailwind classes, and ZERO HTML assumptions. It manages accessibility (ARIA attributes), focus traps, and keyboard navigation.

---

## 🚫 MANDATORY RULES & FATAL VIOLATIONS

### 1. NEVER IMPORT `@media-sdk/core` OR PEXELS TYPES INSIDE `@media-sdk/ui-react`
- ❌ **WRONG**:
  ```tsx
  // Inside @media-sdk/ui-react hook:
  import { PexelsPhoto } from '@media-sdk/core'; // FATAL: Breaks headless UI decoupling
  ```
- ✅ **RIGHT**: Headless hooks MUST accept generic numbers/counts and un-opinionated callback handlers:
  ```tsx
  export function useGrid(options: { fetchNextPage?: () => void }) { ... }
  ```

### 2. NEVER ADD INLINE STYLES OR CLASSNAMES INSIDE HEADLESS HOOKS
- ❌ **WRONG**:
  ```tsx
  const getContainerProps = () => ({
    style: { display: 'grid', gridTemplateColumns: 'repeat(3, 1fr)' }, // FATAL: Opinionated CSS styling in headless package
    className: 'grid-container'
  });
  ```
- ✅ **RIGHT**: Return pure ARIA and event handler prop-getters:
  ```tsx
  const getContainerProps = (userProps) => mergeProps({
    role: 'grid',
    'aria-busy': isLoading
  }, userProps);
  ```

---

## 💡 USAGE PATTERNS & CODE EXAMPLES

### 1. Infinite Grid Hook: `useGrid`
```tsx
import { useGrid } from '@media-sdk/ui-react';

function CustomGrid({ items, onLoadMore, hasMore, loading }) {
  const { getContainerProps, getItemProps, getSentinelProps } = useGrid({
    fetchNextPage: onLoadMore,
    hasNextPage: hasMore,
    isLoading: loading,
  });

  return (
    <div {...getContainerProps({ className: 'my-custom-css-grid' })}>
      {items.map((item, index) => (
        <div key={item.id} {...getItemProps(index, { className: 'my-grid-card' })}>
          <img src={item.imageUrl} alt={item.title} />
        </div>
      ))}
      <div {...getSentinelProps()} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 2. Focus-Trapped Lightbox Hook: `useLightbox`
```tsx
import { useLightbox } from '@media-sdk/ui-react';

function CustomLightbox({ items }) {
  const {
    isOpen,
    activeIndex,
    open,
    close,
    getOverlayProps,
    getContentProps,
    getCloseButtonProps,
    getNextButtonProps,
    getPrevButtonProps
  } = useLightbox({ totalItems: items.length });

  if (!isOpen) return null;

  return (
    <div {...getOverlayProps({ className: 'modal-backdrop' })}>
      <div {...getContentProps({ className: 'modal-body' })}>
        <img src={items[activeIndex].url} alt="" />
        <button {...getPrevButtonProps()}>Prev</button>
        <button {...getNextButtonProps()}>Next</button>
        <button {...getCloseButtonProps()}>Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```
